  "summary": "postinstall beacon exfiltrates host identifiers to webhook.site inbox",
  "details": "The package declares a `postinstall` script that runs `main.js` on every `npm install`. `main.js` collects installer host identifiers via `os.hostname()`, `os.userInfo()`, `os.platform()`, `os.arch()`, `process.cwd()`, Node version, and the lifecycle event name, and POSTs them as JSON to a hardcoded webhook.site inbox at `https://webhook.site/13d98b4a-1999-4ec7-92c9-0697c259ca05`. The payload carries a `src: 'mesbah-PoC'` tag. The package has no advertised feature that would require sending installer identity to an anonymous webhook collector.",
